    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">ALLERTON LOCAL KNOWLEDGE</span>
      <h2>Emergency Plumbing in Allerton. What L18 Properties Need.</h2>
      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 0.9rem;">Allerton has a wide mix of homes. There are Victorian semis in the streets around Allerton Road. There are large 1930s detached houses, and newer estates further south. L18 is one of the most well-off postcodes in Liverpool. Most homes are owner-occupied. Many are family homes with more than one bathroom and a kitchen extension.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 0.9rem;">Extensions often cause plumbing problems in Allerton. The new pipes were usually fitted to a fair standard. But no one checked if the old system could cope. So we see pipes that are too small, low pressure and water hammer (banging pipes). We check the whole system before we suggest any work.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 0.9rem;">We also do <a href="/showers-liverpool" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">shower installations</a> and <a href="/radiators-liverpool" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">radiator upgrades</a> for Allerton homes. And we cover emergency call-outs 24/7 across L18.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


