      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Allerton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>The first hour is £120 on weekdays, 9am to 4pm. It is £150 on weekday evenings, nights and weekends. It is £180 on bank holidays. There is no call-out fee. Parts are at cost. If the job needs more time, we price it before we carry on. You get a written price before we start.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Allerton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We guarantee a 30 minute response across Allerton L18. A real person answers the phone 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. There is no voicemail. We send an engineer as soon as you call.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Our Gas Safe registered engineers do all our gas work. By law, anyone doing gas work must be on the Gas Safe Register. You can check our registration at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We give you the right paperwork for any gas work we do.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work in Allerton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All our work has a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fix in Allerton fails within 12 months because of our work, we come back and put it right free.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS</span>&nbsp; What should I do if I smell gas in my Allerton home?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Turn off the gas at the meter straight away. Open all the doors and windows. Do not use any electrical switches. Get everyone out of the house. Call Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999. This is the national gas emergency line and it is open 24/7. Once their engineer has made it safe, call us on <a href="tel:01515580334">0151 558 0334</a>. We will check the whole gas system and do any repairs.</p></div></details>
